  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Quadeer Hussain vs The State Of Telangana on 16 February, 2022 Author: P.Naveen Rao Bench: P Naveen Rao, G.Radha Rani HON'BLE SRI JUSTICE P.NAVEEN RAO AND HON'BLE SMT Dr.JUSTICE G.RADHA RANI WRIT PETITION No.29573 of 2021 Date:16.02.2022 Between: Quadeer Hussaian S/o.Basheer Hussain, Aged about 31 yrs, Occu : Driver, R/o.H.No.4-2-82/2, Zainulabideen Galli, Bhainsa Mandal, Bhainsa, Adilabad District, .....Petitioner",
    "facts": "2. This writ petition is instituted by the brother of detenu Mohammed Ahmed Hussain, challenging the order of detention dated 15.07.2021 made under Section 3 (2) of the Telangana Prevention of Dangerous Activities of Bootleggers, Dacoits, Drug-Offenders, Goondas, Immoral Traffic Offenders, Land-Grabbers, Spurious Seed Offenders, Insecticide Offenders, Fertilizer Offenders, Food Adulteration Offenders, Fake Documents Offenders, Scheduled Commodities Offenders, Forest Offenders, Gaming Offenders, Sexual Offenders, Explosive Substances Offenders, Arms Offenders, Cyber Crime offenders and While Collar or Financial Offenders Act, 1986 (Act 1 of 1986). 3. Heard Ms. Ayesha Mohammed, learned counsel for the petitioner and learned Government Pleader for home. 4. The order of detention is resorted to on the ground of involvement in five crimes recently by the detenu. The detaining authority also took note of the fact that the detenu was in the habit of committing similar crimes and 44 crimes were registered against him between the year 2018 and 2021 in different police stations of Nizamabad Police Commissionerate, on the allegation of theft of two wheeler motor cycles. It appears the detenu was also involved in the crime registered under Narcotic Drugs And Psychotropic Substances, Act, 1985 in I-Town Police Station, Nizamabad and later he was acquitted.",
